\* All TLC check configs for AntflyDerivedReplay.tla, one section per check.
\* Sections are verbatim TLC config syntax; the build extracts them
\* (scripts/tla-cfg.sh). Section names match the make-target check ids.

==== positive tier=fast
\* TLC config for AntflyDerivedReplay.tla

SPECIFICATION FairSpec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyMissingHintPublication = FALSE
    Indexes = {"dense"}
    MaxSeq = 2

INVARIANTS
    TypeOK
    ReplayPublicationOrdered
    WatermarksOrdered
    LatestHintMetadataHasHintRows
    NoAppliedSkipsTargetedReplay
    QueryTargetNeverObservesBeyondSafeApplied
    TruncationKeepsNeededReplay
    ReplayAllFallbackPreventsFalseEmptyAdvance
    Safety

PROPERTIES
    CatchupEventuallyCompletes

==== Bad
\* Expected-failure config for AntflyDerivedReplay.tla.
\*
\* Enables a mutant where one matching replay-all row is published without its
\* hint-lane row. The fallback protects an entirely empty/unavailable lane, but
\* a later hint-lane match can still advance past this hidden hole.
\* Pinned to the specific semantic invariant this mutant must violate.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyMissingHintPublication = TRUE
    Indexes = {"dense"}
    MaxSeq = 2

INVARIANTS
    NoAppliedSkipsTargetedReplay

==== heavy tier=manual
\* Heavier config for AntflyDerivedReplay.tla.
\*
\* This keeps the deeper two-index/state-space coverage out of the fast tier.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyMissingHintPublication = FALSE
    Indexes = {"dense", "fulltext"}
    MaxSeq = 3

INVARIANTS
    Safety

==== heavy-depth tier=heavy
\* Depth-focused heavier config for AntflyDerivedReplay.tla.
\*
\* Keeps one index but raises MaxSeq to cover longer replay, metadata,
\* catch-up, and truncation interleavings without the full two-index cross
\* product from AntflyDerivedReplay-heavy.cfg.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyMissingHintPublication = FALSE
    Indexes = {"dense"}
    MaxSeq = 3

INVARIANTS
    Safety

==== heavy-multi-index tier=heavy
\* Multi-index heavier config for AntflyDerivedReplay.tla.
\*
\* Keeps MaxSeq at the fast bound but enables both representative derived
\* indexes to cover cross-index catch-up, hint-lane availability, bulk-session,
\* and truncation interactions without the full MaxSeq=3 cross product.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyMissingHintPublication = FALSE
    Indexes = {"dense", "fulltext"}
    MaxSeq = 2

INVARIANTS
    Safety
